workedExamples.question_text:
The histogram represents a discrete random variable $X$. Is its distribution uniform? Explain.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=12mm,y=100mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black,->] (-0.7,0)--(3.8,0);
\draw[black,->] (-0.7,0)--(-0.7,0.34);
\foreach \y in {0.1,0.2,0.3} {
\draw[draw={rgb,255:red,204;green,204;blue,204}] (-0.7,\y)--(3.5,\y);
\draw[black] (-0.78,\y)--(-0.7,\y);
\path (-0.82,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\y$};
}
\foreach \x/\h in {0/0.2,1/0.3,2/0.3,3/0.2} {
\draw[black] (\x-0.5,0) rectangle (\x+0.5,\h);
\path (\x,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\x$};
}
\path (-0.7,0.34) node[above] {$P(X=x)$};
\path (3.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.question_text:
The histogram shows the distribution of $X$, the number of tickets sold at a booth in one hour.
Is $X$ uniformly distributed?
Explain.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,4.4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(8.6,0);
\foreach \y/\lbl in {1/0.1,2/0.2,3/0.3} {\draw (-0.2,\y)--(0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,\y) {$\lbl$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,0) {$0$};
\draw (0.75,0) rectangle (2.25,2.5);
\draw (2.55,0) rectangle (4.05,2.5);
\draw (4.35,0) rectangle (5.85,3);
\draw (6.15,0) rectangle (7.65,2);
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (1.5,0) {$2$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (3.3,0) {$4$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (5.1,0) {$6$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (6.9,0) {$8$};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.4,1.7) {$P(X=x)$};
\node[below] at (4.2,-1.0) {Tickets sold};
\node at (4.2,4.1) {Tickets sold per hour};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
